    "id": "NSIDC-0810_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The QuikSCAT/SeaWinds product (NSIDC-0810) provides Ku-band radar backscatter measurements  Sigma Nought (\u03c3\u2070, Sigma0) collected by the SeaWinds scatterometer instruments aboard the QuikSCAT and ADEOS-2 satellites. Seawinds aboard QuikSCAT collected \u03c3\u2070 measurements from September 1999 through June 2009, while SeaWinds aboard ADEOS-2 collected \u03c3\u2070 measurements from April through October 2003. SeaWinds was designed to provide \u03c3\u2070 measurements for estimating near-surface ocean vector winds, but it also collected \u03c3\u2070 measurements over land and ice that are useful for studies of the cryosphere, climate, vegetation, and other geophysical processes.\n\nNSIDC-0810 includes Level 3 gridded, twice-daily radar backscatter data collected at 13.4 GHz for two radar channels (horizontal transmit-horizontal receive[HH] and vertical transmit-vertical receive[VV]). The data are gridded to EASE-Grid 2.0 azimuthal and cylindrical projections (Brodzik et al., 2012; Brodzik et al., 2014) at 25 km and 3.125 km grid spacings. The 25 km products are generated using drop-in-the-bucket (DIB) gridding, while the 3.125 km products use enhanced-resolution Scatterometer Image Reconstruction (SIR) techniques (Early and Long, 2001).",
